#X obj 674 11 metro.seq;
#X obj 230 93 cnv 1 535 292 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 98 Easy way to build beat machines;
#X text 240 123 The object runs a steady metronome with a fixed interval
\, but only produces a bang on those beats where the corresponding
element of the pattern list is 1\. Elements equal to 0 produce silence
on that beat. The pattern is looped automatically. The interval can
be changed at any time through the second inlet \, and a new pattern
can be sent to the third inlet.;
#X text 240 239 Use case in algorithmic composition: polymetric structure.
A composer can build several [metro.seq] objects with patterns of different
lengths \, for example 5 \, 7 and 11 steps \, all running at the same
interval. Because the lengths are mutually prime \, the resulting composite
rhythm never repeats itself exactly within a reasonable time \, producing
a slowly evolving polyrhythmic texture that is typical of process-based
music.;
